#: R/cp_analysis.R
msgid "Membership c-statistic"
msgstr "Estadístic c de pertinença"

#: R/cplogistic.b.R
msgid ""
"Membership c-statistic: how well the predictors and the outcome distinguish "
"validation from development rows (Debray et al. 2015). Near 0.5: similar "
"case-mix (reproducibility); high: different populations (transportability). "
"A larger SD of the linear predictor means a more heterogeneous case-mix, "
"which by itself raises the AUC."
msgstr "Estadístic c de pertinença: en quina mesura els predictors i el desenllaç distingeixen les files de validació de les de desenvolupament (Debray et al. 2015). Prop de 0,5: case-mix similar (reproductibilitat); alt: poblacions diferents (transportabilitat). Una DE més gran del predictor lineal indica un case-mix més heterogeni, que per si sol augmenta l'AUC."

#: R/cpcox.b.R
msgid ""
"Membership c-statistic: how well the predictors and the outcome distinguish "
"validation from development rows (Debray et al. 2015). Near 0.5: similar "
"case-mix (reproducibility); high: different populations (transportability). "
"A larger SD of the linear predictor means a more heterogeneous case-mix, "
"which by itself raises the concordance."
msgstr "Estadístic c de pertinença: en quina mesura els predictors i el desenllaç distingeixen les files de validació de les de desenvolupament (Debray et al. 2015). Prop de 0,5: case-mix similar (reproductibilitat); alt: poblacions diferents (transportabilitat). Una DE més gran del predictor lineal indica un case-mix més heterogeni, que per si sol augmenta la concordança."

#: R/cplinear.b.R
msgid ""
"Membership c-statistic: how well the predictors and the outcome distinguish "
"validation from development rows (Debray et al. 2015). Near 0.5: similar "
"case-mix (reproducibility); high: different populations (transportability). "
"A larger SD of the predictions means a more heterogeneous case-mix, which by "
"itself raises the R²."
